48a7256a926f79bbd491"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2002364 - [ci] Update url for mfpr-3.1.4 fetch, r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau a=release\n\nLooks like mpfr.org started redirecting to https but their TLS setup is\nbroken. We found an alternative hosted on ftp.gnu.org.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274138\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "ce806849879560e8ea3e440991416617d16ba7c6", "git_parents": ["676834c1f9c095aed0fef90c129c8d3de65068f8"], "node": "8968eb29a34d1ce4895215d34ae984973d092571", "parents": ["2bed89d69344f53aaf7f675839516a74f9716302"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Landry Breuil \u003clandry@openbsd.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999324 - dlopen(\"libnotify.so\") on OpenBSD to fix notifications r=saschanaz, a=RyanVM\n\nOn OpenBSD, the library versioning is controled by the portstree, and\ndlopen()/ld.so knows how to find the most recent version by being given no\nsuffix.\n\nNSPR's pr_LoadLibrary() is patched on OpenBSD to cope (cf bug #650772) but that\ndoesn't work when dlopen() is used directly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D272518\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/nsAlertsIconListener.cpp"], "git_node": "27aa69408c4afc2701d1edc36c2952b301254e7c", "git_parents": ["ce806849879560e8ea3e440991416617d16ba7c6"], "node": "ddadadcb0d4dd2ca66efb865865acb05d5664c6f", "parents": ["8968eb29a34d1ce4895215d34ae984973d092571"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001533 - Fix Startup Crash in [@ mozilla::ViaductRequest::LaunchRequest]. r=adw a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273535\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/viaduct/ViaductRequest.cpp"], "git_node": "88fff665caa689acff7e8101c28ab81f2270f9ae", "git_parents": ["27aa69408c4afc2701d1edc36c2952b301254e7c"], "node": "19af8b9a7271c174d2e9456657849491b1995397", "parents": ["ddadadcb0d4dd2ca66efb865865acb05d5664c6f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1765306006, "git_changesets": ["676834c1f9c095aed0fef90c129c8d3de65068f8", "ce806849879560e8ea3e440991416617d16ba7c6", "27aa69408c4afc2701d1edc36c2952b301254e7c", "88fff665caa689acff7e8101c28ab81f2270f9ae"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "385": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2002697 - Only attempt to destroy GMP process once if crashes during shutdown.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nWe need to let GMPParent::ActorDestroy complete the teardown when we\ncrash during the shutdown handshake attempting to get the profiler, if\npresent, from the GMP process.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274242\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274426\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp"], "git_node": "012383578873ef9f6b6023a3a459bd6714eacb41", "git_parents": ["88fff665caa689acff7e8101c28ab81f2270f9ae"], "node": "d05b1140d6be277df2c5f55fb4c7b1dd4b348282", "parents": ["19af8b9a7271c174d2e9456657849491b1995397"], "tags": []}], "date": 1765388582, "git_changesets": ["012383578873ef9f6b6023a3a459bd6714eacb41"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "386": {"changesets": [{"author": "Artur Iunusov \u003caiunusov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2002517 - disable dom.workers.timeoutmanager in esr140, r=smaug a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\n- let's stick to the old timeoutmanager implementation in this esr\n- and start using it in next esr (where pref is removed)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274675\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "4a5197c5d883800e830d5541d36d58d4be3ff0da", "git_parents": ["012383578873ef9f6b6023a3a459bd6714eacb41"], "node": "3e2bc3a0c0713653c32a17d521258fbde35d4a24", "parents": ["d05b1140d6be277df2c5f